#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:41
msgid "Third-party Tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:43
msgid ""
"There are a number of third-party utilities which aim to address this issue. "
"These typically provide an installer, let Syncthing start automatically, and "
"a more polished user experience (e.g. by behaving as a \"proper\" Windows "
"application, rather than forcing you to start your browser to interact with "
"Syncthing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:49
msgid ""
":ref:`Windows GUI Wrappers <contrib-windows>`, :ref:`Cross-platform GUI "
"Wrappers <contrib-all>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:52
msgid "Start on Login"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:54
msgid ""
"Starting Syncthing on login, without a console window or browser opening on "
"start, is relatively easy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:57
msgid ""
"Find the correct link of the Windows binary from the `Syncthing website "
"<https://github.com/syncthing/syncthing/releases>`__ (choose **amd64** if "
"you have a 64-bit version of Windows)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:60
msgid ""
"Extract the files in the folder (``syncthing-windows-*``) in the zip to the "
"folder ``C:\\syncthing``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:62
msgid "Go to the ``C:\\syncthing`` folder, make a file named ``syncthing.bat``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:64
msgid ""
"Right-click the file and choose **Edit**. The file should open in Notepad or "
"your default text editor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:66
msgid ""
"Paste the following command into the file and save the changes: ``start "
"\"Syncthing\" syncthing.exe -no-console -no-browser``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:68
msgid "Right-click on ``syncthing.bat`` and press \"Create Shortcut\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:69
msgid ""
"Right-click the shortcut file ``syncthing.bat - Shortcut`` and click **Copy**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:71
msgid ""
"Click **Start**, click **All Programs**, then click **Startup**. Right-click "
"on **Startup** then click **Open**. |Setup Screenshot|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:317
msgid "Setup Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:74
msgid ""
"Paste the shortcut (right-click in the folder and choose **Paste**, or press "
"``CTRL+V``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:77
msgid ""
"Syncthing will now automatically start the next time you open a new Windows "
"session. No console or browser window will pop-up. Access the interface by "
"browsing to http://localhost:8384/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:81
msgid ""
"If you prefer slower indexing but a more responsive system during scans, "
"copy the following command instead of the command in step 5::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:84
msgid "start \"Syncthing\" /low syncthing.exe -no-console -no-browser"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:87
msgid "Run as a service independent of user login"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:90
msgid ""
"There are important security considerations with this approach. If you do "
"not secure Syncthing's GUI (and REST API), then **any** process running with "
"**any** permissions can read/write **any** file on your filesystem, by "
"opening a connection with Syncthing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:95
msgid ""
"Therefore, you **must** ensure that you set a GUI password, or run Syncthing "
"as an unprivileged user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:98
msgid ""
"With the above configuration, Syncthing only starts when a user logs on to "
"the machine. This is not optimal on servers where a machine can run long "
"times after a reboot without anyone logged in. In this case it is best to "
"create a service that runs as soon as Windows starts. This can be achieved "
"using NSSM, the \"Non-Sucking Service Manager\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:103
msgid ""
"Note that starting Syncthing on login is the preferred approach for almost "
"any end-user scenario. The only scenario where running Syncthing as a "
"service makes sense is for (mostly) headless servers, administered by a "
"sysadmin who knows enough to understand the security implications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:108
msgid ""
"Download and extract `nssm <http://nssm.cc/download>`__ to a folder where it "
"can stay. The NSSM executable performs administration as well as executing "
"as the Windows service so it will need to be kept in a suitable location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:109
msgid ""
"From an administrator Command Prompt, CD to the NSSM folder and run ``nssm."
"exe install syncthing``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:110
msgid "Application Tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:112
msgid ""
"Set *Path* to your ``syncthing.exe`` and enter ``-no-restart -no-browser -"
"home=\"<path to your Syncthing folder>\"`` as Arguments. Note: Logging is "
"set later on. ``-logfile`` here will not be applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:113
msgid "|Windows NSSM Configuration Screenshot|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:316
msgid "Windows NSSM Configuration Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:114
msgid "Details Tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:116
msgid ""
"Optional: Set *Startup type* to *Automatic (Delayed Start)* to delay the "
"start of Syncthing when the system first boots, to improve boot speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:117
msgid "Log On Tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:119
msgid ""
"Enter the user account to run Syncthing as. This user needs to have access "
"to all the synced folders. You can leave this as *Local System* but doing so "
"poses security risks. Setting this to your Windows user account will reduce "
"this; ideally create a dedicated user account with minimal permissions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:120
msgid "Process Tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:122
msgid ""
"Optional: Change priority to *Low* if you want a more responsive system at "
"the cost of somewhat longer sync time when the system is busy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:123
msgid "Optional: To enable logging enable \"Console window\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:124
msgid "Shutdown Tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:126
msgid ""
"To ensure Syncthing is shut down gracefully select all of the checkboxes and "
"set all *Timeouts* to *10000ms*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:127
msgid "Exit Actions Tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:129
msgid ""
"Set *Restart Action* to *Stop service (oneshot mode)*. Specific settings are "
"used later for handling Syncthing exits, restarts and upgrades."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:130
msgid "I/O Tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:132
msgid ""
"Optional: To enable logging set *Output (stdout)* to the file desired for "
"logging. The *Error* field will be automatically set to the same file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:133
msgid "File Rotation Tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:135
msgid "Optional: Set the rotation settings to your preferences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:136
msgid "Click the *Install Service* Button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:137
msgid ""
"To ensure that Syncthing exits, restarts and upgrades are handled correctly "
"by the Windows service manager, some final settings are needed. Execute "
"these in the same Commant Prompt:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:139
msgid "``nssm set syncthing AppExit Default Exit``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:140
msgid "``nssm set syncthing AppExit 0 Exit``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:141
msgid "``nssm set syncthing AppExit 3 Restart``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:142
msgid "``nssm set syncthing AppExit 4 Restart``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:143
msgid "Start the service via ``sc start syncthing`` in the Command Prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:144
msgid ""
"Connect to the Syncthing UI, enable HTTPS, and set a secure username and "
"password."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:147
msgid "Mac OS X"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:150
msgid "Using `homebrew <http://brew.sh>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:152
msgid "``brew install syncthing``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:153
msgid ""
"Follow the information presented by ``brew`` to autostart Syncthing using "
"launchctl."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:156
msgid "Without homebrew"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:158
msgid ""
"Download and extract Syncthing for Mac: https://github.com/syncthing/"
"syncthing/releases/latest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:161
msgid ""
"Copy the syncthing binary (the file you would open to launch Syncthing) into "
"a directory called ``bin`` in your home directory i.e. into /home/<username>/"
"bin. If \"bin\" does not exist, create it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:164
msgid ""
"Open ``syncthing.plist`` located in /etc/macosx-launchd. Replace the four "
"occurrences of /Users/USERNAME with your actual home directory location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:165
msgid ""
"Copy the ``syncthing.plist`` file to ``~/Library/LaunchAgents``. If you have "
"trouble finding this location select the \"Go\" menu in Finder and choose "
"\"Go to folder...\" and then type ``~/Library/LaunchAgents``. Copying to ~/"
"Library/LaunchAgents will require admin password in most cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:170
msgid ""
"Log out and back in again. Or, if you do not want to log out, you can run "
"this command in terminal: ``launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/syncthing."
"plist``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:174
msgid ""
"**Note:** You probably want to turn off \"Start Browser\" in the web GUI "
"settings to avoid it opening a browser window on each login. Then, to access "
"the GUI type 127.0.0.1:8384 (by default) into Safari."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:179
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:182
msgid "On Ubuntu-like systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:184
msgid "Launch the program 'Startup Applications'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:185
msgid "Click 'Add'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:186
msgid "Fill out the form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:188
msgid "Name: Syncthing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:189
msgid ""
"Command: ``/path/to/syncthing/binary -no-browser -home=\"/home/your\\_user/."
"config/syncthing\"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:192
msgid "Using Supervisord"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:194
msgid "Add the following to your ``/etc/supervisord.conf`` file::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:196
msgid ""
"[program:syncthing]\n"
"command = /path/to/syncthing/binary -no-browser -home=\"/home/some_user/."
"config/syncthing\"\n"
"directory = /home/some_user/\n"
"autorestart = True\n"
"user = some_user\n"
"environment = STNORESTART=\"1\", HOME=\"/home/some_user\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:204
msgid "Using systemd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:206
msgid ""
"systemd is a suite of system management daemons, libraries, and utilities "
"designed as a central management and configuration platform for the Linux "
"computer operating system. It also offers users the ability to manage "
"services under the user's control with a per-user systemd instance, enabling "
"users to start, stop, enable, and disable their own units. Service files for "
"systemd are provided by Syncthing and can be found in `etc/linux-systemd "
"<https://github.com/syncthing/syncthing/tree/master/etc/linux-systemd>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:215
msgid ""
"You have two primary options: You can set up Syncthing as a system service, "
"or a user service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:218
msgid ""
"Running Syncthing as a system service ensures that Syncthing is run at "
"startup even if the Syncthing user has no active session. Since the system "
"service keeps Syncthing running even without an active user session, it is "
"intended to be used on a *server*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:223
msgid ""
"Running Syncthing as a user service ensures that Syncthing only starts after "
"the user has logged into the system (e.g., via the graphical login screen, "
"or ssh). Thus, the user service is intended to be used on a *(multiuser) "
"desktop computer*. It avoids unnecessarily running Syncthing instances."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:228
msgid ""
"Several distros (including arch linux) ship the needed service files with "
"the Syncthing package. If your distro provides a systemd service file for "
"Syncthing, you can skip step 2 when you setting up either the system service "
"or the user service, as described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:234
msgid "How to set up a system service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:236
msgid "Create the user who should run the service, or choose an existing one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:237
msgid ""
"Copy the ``Syncthing/etc/system/syncthing@.service`` file into the `load "
"path of the system instance <http://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/"
"systemd.unit.html#Unit%20Load%20Path>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:240
msgid ""
"Enable and start the service. Replace \"myuser\" with the actual Syncthing "
"user after the ``@``::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:243
msgid ""
"systemctl enable syncthing@myuser.service\n"
"systemctl start syncthing@myuser.service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:247
msgid "How to set up a user service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:249
msgid ""
"Create the user who should run the service, or choose an existing one. "
"*Probably this will be your own user account.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:251
msgid ""
"Copy the ``Syncthing/etc/user/syncthing.service`` file into the `load path "
"of the user instance <http://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/"
"systemd.unit.html#Unit%20Load%20Path>`__. To do this without root privileges "
"you can just use this folder under your home directory: ``~/.config/systemd/"
"user/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:256
msgid "Enable and start the service::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:258
msgid ""
"systemctl --user enable syncthing.service\n"
"systemctl --user start syncthing.service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:262
msgid "Checking the service status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:264
msgid ""
"To check if Syncthing runs properly you can use the ``status`` subcommand. "
"To check the status of a system service::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:267
msgid "systemctl status syncthing@myuser.service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:269
msgid "To check the status of a user service::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:271
msgid "systemctl --user status syncthing.service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:274
msgid "Using the journal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:276
msgid ""
"Systemd logs everything into the journal, so you can easily access Syncthing "
"log messages. In both of the following examples, ``-e`` tells the pager to "
"jump to the very end, so that you see the most recent logs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:280
msgid "To see the logs for the system service::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:282
msgid "journalctl -e -u syncthing@myuser.service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:284
msgid "To see the logs for the user service::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:286
msgid "journalctl -e --user-unit=syncthing.service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:289
msgid "Permissions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:291
msgid ""
"If you enabled the ``Ignore Permissions`` option in the Syncthing client's "
"folder settings, then you will also need to add the line ``UMask=0002`` (or "
"any other `umask setting <http://www.tech-faq.com/umask.html>` you like) in "
"the ``[Service]`` section of the ``syncthing@.service`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:297
msgid "Debugging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:299
msgid ""
"If you are asked on the bugtracker to start Syncthing with specific "
"environment variables it will not work the normal way. Systemd isolates each "
"service and it cannot access global environment variables. The solution is "
"to add the variables to the service file instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:304
msgid "To edit the system service, run::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:306
msgid "systemctl edit syncthing@myuser.service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:308
msgid "To edit the user service, run::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:310
msgid "systemctl --user edit syncthing.service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/autostart.rst:312
msgid ""
"This will create an additional configuration file automatically and you can "
"define (or overwrite) further service parameters like e.g. "
"``Environment=STTRACE=model``."
msgstr ""
